        "date": "2026-11-13T22:04:48Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(bore): refuse a bore too wide for its ring, and keep it out of Detect holes\n\nThe Bore ride is a centre dive, one radial sweep and one ring on the\nwall. Past 3 x tool diameter + 2 x stock to leave the dive's disc and\nthe ring's band no longer meet, so a through bore freed a core (the\nissue's Ø74.3 bore with a 4 mm tool left a Ø66 disc) and still\ngenerated and verified ok.\n\n- motion: the bore kernel refuses such a hole at its door with the\n  hole, cutter, ring radius, core size and limit named;\n  max_bore_diameter() states the limit once.\n- app: detect_holes on a Bore op keeps only the holes its tool clears\n  and names each one left out (DetectedHoles.skipped); all too wide is\n  a refusal. MCP detect_holes answers `skipped`; the GUI status line\n  says the same.\n- Pins: bore_core_tests (refusal numbers, the limit, floor coverage\n  law), tests/bore_core.rs (MCP), detect_holes_note_tests (GUI).\n\nFixes #1556\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
